WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:01.789
Far out, giants.

00:02.489 --> 00:09.269
Further out, where it was cold, ice and gas could gather too, and that is where the giant planets formed.

00:09.719 --> 00:19.598
Jupiter took most of what was left over after the Sun: more than twice as much material as every other planet, moon and rock put together.
